From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:45:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] FEXCore, ARM64EC: x86 execute breakpoints on Wine's
 ARM64EC

FEXCore gets the steamac execute-breakpoint support: the JIT checks each
instruction address that is armed as an execute breakpoint in some thread
and raises #DB (SIGTRAP, trapno 1, si_code TRAP_HWBKPT) before it runs,
with DR6 status bits and EFLAGS.RF semantics (a pending RF skips one hit).

The ARM64EC frontend keeps DR0-DR7 per thread and detours Wine's ARM64EC
NtSetContextThread/NtGetContextThread, whose x64 context conversion drops
the debug registers (context_x64_to_arm only maps the general purpose
state). ResetToConsistentState fills DR0-DR7, DR6 and RF into the x64
context the guest exception handlers see, since Wine builds that context
inside ntdll after the emulator's hooks. Hooks are installed only under
Wine.

InvalidationTracker: skip a re-entrant invalidation. FEX's own
__builtin___clear_cache goes through NtFlushInstructionCache on Windows,
Wine's ARM64EC ntdll calls back into BTCpu64FlushInstructionCache for it,
and the delinker in InvalidateCodeBuffersCodeRange does the flush while
CodeInvalidationMutex is held, which deadlocked. The nested range is host
JIT code, not guest code.

tools/dr-test on CrossOver 27 Preview (wine-11.17, FEX ARM64EC):
RESULT PASS, phase A and B, DR6 0xffff0ff1, EFlags.RF set.

steamac local patch (msfs2024-steamac patches/fex/steamac-darwin-on-02e24ca5c.patch). Not for upstream.
